        {
          "properties": {
            "altText": {
              "expr": {
                "Literal": {
                  "Value": "'The share of available marks earned on work that has been marked, how much of the handed-in work has been marked, how many learners stand behind that share, and the gap in percentage points between the strongest and weakest quarter of them. The school, year group and subject slicers apply. Leave more than one subject selected and this figure adds up marks from schemes that were never on one scale, so keep it to a single subject when the number is meant to be read. The month and date slicers do not: the only date on a piece of set work is the class due date, so marked work is shown for the whole reporting period. The chart below breaks the score down by school.'"
